  "heat": 2,
  "text": "Abigail stopped a war with supplies and a speech. First Samuel twenty five. David's men had protected Nabal's shepherds, and when David sends ten young men to ask for provision, Nabal insults him and sends them away with nothing. David straps on his sword and takes four hundred men. He is riding out to wipe out a household. A servant runs to Abigail and tells her everything. And she does not call a meeting. The text says she made haste. Two hundred loaves, two bottles of wine, five dressed sheep, roasted grain, a hundred clusters of raisins, two hundred cakes of figs. She loads it all onto donkeys and rides out to intercept an armed column, without telling her husband. Then she gets down off the donkey, falls on her face, and talks. She takes the blame on herself, tells David that shedding this blood would be a grief and an offence of heart to him later, and asks him to remember her when God has done him good. And David says, blessed be thy advice, and blessed be thou, which hast kept me this day from coming to shed blood. She talked a future king off the ledge.",
